{"text": "REAZ Q. KHAN\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\u2018To seck a water & wastewater treatment/engineering position with he City of Portland, OR.\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n09/05 \u2014 present Volunteer Trainee, CLARK COUNTY PUBLIC WORKS, Vancouver, WA.\n\n\u2018Wastewater treatment plant operations training at Salmon Creek Wastewater Treatment Plant. Training\nareas include Preliminary Treatment, Primary Treatment, Aeration Basin, RAS/WAS Pumping Station,\nSecondary Clarifier, Sludge Treatment, Digester, Solids Processing, Instrumentation & Process Control,\nPLC/SCADA System and Laboratory procedures. Reviewing plant engincering design reports, construction\ndeawings, as-built drawings and ongoing expansion engineering design and construction plans.\n\n01/98- 06/04 Engineering & Technology Manager, GENESIS COMPUTER SYSTEMS, INC., Anaheim, CA.\n\nLed applications engineering and inanufacturing teams for industrial-PC interface solutions for a wide range\nof applications including petroleum drilling machines, chemical process equipment, telecom, access control,\nsecurity /video-surveillance and laboratory instruments. Performed systems integration, compatibility and\nhardware-conffict resolutions, system testing, and application software installation and testing. Compiled\nequipment documentation and technical service manuals. Performed PC network administration for various\noffice environments including CAD, Engineering, Accounting and Office Automation. Provided training\nand technical support to clients and staff. Prepared quotations and proposals, negotiated contract terms,\nprepared manufacturing and assembly schedules, managed costs, billings and collections. Performed\ncustomer management aod relationship development, including dispute resolution with minimal need for\nescalation. Introduced new products, services and upgrades.\n\n11/93 =12/97 Project Manager, AQUAMATCH, INC., Laguna Hills, CA.\n\u2018Managed all project phases of industrial, commercial and community water & wastewatet treatment plant\nmanufacturing from bidding to commissioning and closeout. Prepared estimates, proposals and bid\npackages. Reviewed and interpreted contract terms & conditions. Prepared project schedules and\nproactively addressed potential problems. Evaluated clicat bulletins, field directives & schedule changes and\nperformed associated cost estimates, negotiated settlements, and issued change orders. Performed\nsubcontractor and vendor management functions, including vendor qualification, negotiations, preparation,\nissuance of subcontracts, monitoring subcontractor progress and compliance, and dispute resolution.\nManaged all aspects of procurement, fabrication, installation, testing and commissioning: Oversaw project\nexecution for compliance with contract tetms, specifications, regulatory codes and engineering practices.\nMonitored project schedules, costs/expenses, billings. Communicated project status/progress and finances\nto corporate officers and client and issued alerts related to any actual or anticipated problems. Supervised\nengineering teams for process design, load analysis, system simulation, unit analysis, PFDs, MHBs and\nP&Ds, sizing piping, valves, pumps, designing pressure vessels, reactors, tanks, treatment plant structure\nand supports. Supervised design teams for CAD, 2D/3D modeling of plants using AutoCAD, preparation\nof bills of materials, fabrication and as-built drawings. Supervised systems engineering for instrumentation\nand control systems, instrumentation clusters, PLC based control panels, switchgear and motot control\ncabinets. Projects included 1.2 Million-GPD/1800psi seawater desalination plant, 100 kGPD manufactaring\nwastewater treatment plant, 40 kGPD ultra purity industrial deionization unit, 80K GPD pharmaceutical\n\nPage 1 of 2",
